ratchet_migration_note: `Debug compiler_rt report-all discovery moved from 129 emitting / 314 failing to 130 emitting / 313 failing after aligning the stage-two spill envelope with the 32-slot frame model and accepting pointer phis as 64-bit GPR phi values. The row remains fail-closed. The intByteSize cycle did not move report-all counts, but it advanced the first __udivei5 selector detail from composed-block-call-form to composed-block-spill-slots. This cycle also did not move report-all counts, but it advanced the first __udivei5 selector detail from composed-block-spill-slots to composed-block-spill-loc by making x86_64 FrameIndex a data slot instead of a fixed enum namespace, deriving RSP displacements dynamically through the existing disp8/disp32 encoder, and sizing the composed spill reservation from the allocation plan while preserving the INBOX-4 single-frame authority invariant.`

